# Tests

`./mvnw test` must pass with no PostgreSQL server, no Docker, and no network. Database
tests start an embedded PostgreSQL (`io.zonky.test:embedded-postgres`) and run Flyway
against it; anything that would reach the internet is mocked.

- Web tests use `@WebMvcTest(controllers = ...)` with `@Import` of `SecurityConfig` and
  `GlobalExceptionHandler`, services replaced by `@MockitoBean`, and configuration
  supplied through `@TestPropertySource` — see
  @src/test/java/com/kindlerss/web/AppControllerSecurityTest.java.
- Authenticated requests use `@WithMockUser(username = "kindle")`, and a `POST` needs
  `.with(csrf())`. Keep at least one test asserting that a `POST` without a token is
  rejected.
- Test classes and methods are package-private, no `public`.
- Method names are sentences describing the behavior, not the method under test:
  `sendingCannotBeTalkedIntoLeavingTheApp`, `advanceOnAnUnreadListStaysOnTheSamePage`.
- Assert on what the user gets — the rendered markup, the redirect target, the number of
  rows changed — rather than on internal calls, and use `verify` only where the side
  effect is the point (mail sent, nothing marked read).
- New behavior in the security helpers (`safeRedirect`, `safeHttpUrl`,
  `SafeHttpClient.isBlockedAddress`) needs a direct unit test for the rejected case, not
  only the accepted one.
